    answer: 'Continue CPAP at 10 cm H2O for the remainder of the study and document the treatment-emergent central sleep apnea. Do not immediately switch to adaptive servo-ventilation during the first titration night. Treatment-emergent CSA resolves spontaneously in the majority of patients (50-80%) with continued CPAP use over weeks to months. Document the findings in the report, recommend CPAP at 10 cm H2O, and schedule a follow-up in 2-3 months with a repeat study if central events persist clinically. If symptoms continue, ASV can be considered at that time.',
